<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ntare V of Burundi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1947">1947</a>–<a href="/years/1972">1972</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Charles Ndizeye</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ntare-v">Ntare V</a>, born Charles Ndizeye, was the last king of Burundi. He deposed his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwambutsa-iv">Mwambutsa IV</a> in July 1966 and was crowned, but in November of the same year his prime minister, Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michel-micombero">Michel Micombero</a>, overthrew him and proclaimed a republic. Returning from exile in 1972, he was arrested and killed during the violence of that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ntare-v-of-burundi.jpg" alt="Ntare V of Burundi" width="320" height="417" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Associated Press · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ntare_V_of_Burundi_(1966).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
